H8315.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 4:22; 
son of: Shelah (H7956); 
brother of: Er (H6147H), Laadah (H3935), Jokim (H3137) and Joash (H3101K) 
§ Saraph = "to burn"
a Judaite, son of Shelah who ruled in Moab

H8325.def:
A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Samuel 23:33; 
father of: Ahiam (H0279); also called Sachar (KJV: Sacar; NIV: Sakar) at 1 Chroniques 11:35;
Also named: sa.khar (שָׂכָר "Sachar" H7940H) 
§ Sharar = "enemy"
father of Ahiam, one of David's mighty warriors

H8329.def:
A man of the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 7:16; 
son of: Machir (H4353) and Maacah (H4601M); 
brother of: Gilead (H1568H), Peresh (H6570) and Hammolecheth (H4447); 
father of: Ulam (H0198) and Rakem (H7552J) 
§ Sheresh = "root"
son of Machir and grandson of Manasseh

H8339.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 3:19; 
son of: Pedaiah (H6305H); 
brother of: Shimei (H8096J); 
father of: Meshullam (H4918H), Hananiah (H2608L), Shelomith (H8019I), Hashubah (H2807), Ohel (H0169), Berechiah (H1296), Hasadiah (H2619), Jushab-hesed (H3142) and Abiud (G0010); also called Sheshbazzar at Esdras 1:8,11; 5.14,16; KJV: Zorobabel at Matthieu 1:12,13;
Another name of ze.rub.ba.vel (זְרֻבָּבֶ֫ל "Zerubbabel" H2216) 
§ Sheshbazzar = "worshipper of fire"
the prince of Judah at the first return from exile in Babylon; usually identified as the Babylonian name for Zerubbabel

H8340.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 3:19; 
son of: Pedaiah (H6305H); 
brother of: Shimei (H8096J); 
father of: Meshullam (H4918H), Hananiah (H2608L), Shelomith (H8019I), Hashubah (H2807), Ohel (H0169), Berechiah (H1296), Hasadiah (H2619), Jushab-hesed (H3142) and Abiud (G0010); also called Sheshbazzar at Esdras 1:8,11; 5.14,16; KJV: Zorobabel at Matthieu 1:12,13;
Aramaic of ze.rub.ba.vel (זְרֻבָּבֶ֫ל "Zerubbabel" H2216) 
§ Sheshbazzar = "worshipper of fire"
the prince of Judah at the first return from exile in Babylon; usually identified as the Babylonian name for Zerubbabel

H8344.def:
A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Nombres 13:22; 
son of: Anak (H6061); 
brother of: Ahiman (H0289) and Talmai (H8526) 
§ Sheshai = "noble"
son of Anak, one of the giants in the land of Canaan

H8348.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 2:31; 
son of: Ishi (H3469); 
father of: Ahlai (H0304) 
§ Sheshan = "noble"
a Judaite of the families of Hezron and Jerahmeel, son of Ishi and father of Ahlai

H8349.def:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 8:14; 
son of: Beriah (H1283I); 
brother of: Arad (H6166B), Ahio (H0283H), Jeremoth (H3406I), Zebadiah (H2069), Eder (H5738), Michael (H4317L), Ishpah (H3472) and Joha (H3109); 
father of: Ishpan (H3473), Eber (H5677J), Eliel (H0447I), Abdon (H5658I), Zichri (H2147I), Hanan (H2605), Hananiah (H2608O), Elam (H5867), Anthothijah (H6070), Iphdeiah (H3301), Penuel (H6439I) 
§ Shashak = "longing"
a Benjamite, son of Beriah and father of Iphedeiah and Penuel

H8352.def:
A man living at the time before the Flood, first mentioned at Genèse 4:25; 
son of: Adam (H0121) and Eve (H2332); 
brother of: Cain (H7014B) and Abel (H1893); 
father of: Enosh (H0583); also called Sheth (Ketiv: buttock) at Nombres 24:17; 
§ Seth = "compensation"
1) the 3rd son of Adam by Eve
1a) also 'Sheth'

H8364.def:
Someone descended from Shuthelah who was a man of the tribe of Ephraim living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Nombres 26:35; 
son of: Ephraim (H0669); 
brother of: Becher (H1071H), Tahan (H8465), Ezer (H5827), Elead (H0496) and Beriah (H1283H); 
father of: Eran (H6197) and Bered (H1260H)
Group of shu.te.lach (שׁוּתֶ֫לַח "Shuthelah" H7803) 
§ Shuthalhites, of Shuthelah "freshly appointed"
descendants of Shuthelah, son of Ephraim, and of his son of the same name

H8390.def:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 8:35; 
son of: Micah (H4318H); 
brother of: Pithon (H6377), Melech (H4429) and Ahaz (H0271H); also called Tahrea at 1 Chroniques 9:41; 
Also named: tach.re.a (תַּחֲרֵעַ "Tahrea" H8475) 
§ Tarea = "chamber of a neighbour"
a Benjamite, son of Micah of the family of Saul
